Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and how they will probably be used  

PRODUCTS  
• "id": joins to ORDER_ITEMS."product_id".  
• "name": product name that will finally be returned.  
• "cost": unit cost – needed for profit calculation.  
• "retail_price": unit retail price – needed for profit calculation.  
(Condition – none, but will be joined to orders that happened in 2020.)

ORDER_ITEMS  
• "product_id": foreign‑key to PRODUCTS."id".  
• "created_at": micro‑second epoch when the line item was created → used to isolate 2020 sales and to derive the month for chronological ordering.  
• "status": can be used to keep only real sales (e.g. status = 'Complete').  
(Conditions – created_at must fall inside year‑2020; status not 'Cancelled' or 'Returned'.)

Optional (if you want to double‑check quantities)  
• "sale_price": actual selling price.  
• "inventory_item_id": can be joined to INVENTORY_ITEMS but not required for computing profit defined as retail_price – cost.

——————————————————————————————————————————  

Below are 10 exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets (all SELECT‑only, each limited to 20 rows, every identifier enclosed in double quotes). They progress from very simple inspection queries to the final, more complex one that returns—still only as a sample—the product(s) having the lowest profit per 2020 month.

```sql
-- 1) Description: Quick look at product catalogue – names, cost and retail price.
SELECT 
  "id",
  "name",
  "cost",
  "retail_price"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Show profit (retail_price – cost) for a handful of products.
SELECT 
  "id",
  "name",
  "retail_price" - "cost" AS "profit"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Peek at raw order‑item timestamps & statuses.
SELECT 
  "id",
  "order_id",
  "product_id",
  "status",
  "created_at"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Inspect overall min / max order dates (micro‑seconds since epoch).
SELECT 
  MIN("created_at") AS "earliest_created_us",
  MAX("created_at") AS "latest_created_us"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS";
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Distinct year‑month values present in ORDER_ITEMS (uses TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ).
SELECT DISTINCT 
  DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ("created_at" / 1000000.0)) AS "year_month"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"
ORDER BY "year_month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Join a few order items to their products, show profit per line.
SELECT 
  oi."id"                      AS "order_item_id",
  oi."product_id",
  pr."name",
  pr."retail_price",
  pr."cost",
  (pr."retail_price" - pr."cost") AS "profit"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"   oi
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"      pr
  ON pr."id" = oi."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Pull only 2020, successful sales; convert to month; include profit.
SELECT 
  DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at" / 1000000.0)) AS "sale_month",
  oi."product_id",
  pr."name",
  (pr."retail_price" - pr."cost") AS "profit"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"   oi
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"      pr
  ON pr."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND YEAR(TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at" / 1000000.0)) = 2020
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: For each 2020 month, compute the minimum profit observed.
SELECT 
  DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at" / 1000000.0)) AS "sale_month",
  MIN(pr."retail_price" - pr."cost") AS "lowest_profit"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"   oi
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"      pr
  ON pr."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND YEAR(TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at" / 1000000.0)) = 2020
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Retrieve product(s) whose profit equals that minimum per month.
WITH month_min AS (
  SELECT 
    DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at" / 1000000.0)) AS "sale_month",
    MIN(pr."retail_price" - pr."cost") AS "lowest_profit"
  FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
  JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"    pr
    ON pr."id" = oi."product_id"
  WHERE oi."status" = 'Complete'
    AND YEAR(TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at" / 1000000.0)) = 2020
  GROUP BY 1
)
SELECT DISTINCT
  m."sale_month",
  pr."name",
  m."lowest_profit"
FROM month_min                  m
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
  ON DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at" / 1000000.0)) = m."sale_month"
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"     pr
  ON pr."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE (pr."retail_price" - pr."cost") = m."lowest_profit"
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Final list (max 20 rows shown) – product(s) with the LOWEST profit for each month of 2020, ordered chronologically.
WITH month_min AS (
  SELECT 
    DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at" / 1000000.0)) AS "sale_month",
    MIN(pr."retail_price" - pr."cost") AS "lowest_profit"
  FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS" oi
  JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"    pr
    ON pr."id" = oi."product_id"
  WHERE oi."status" = 'Complete'
    AND YEAR(TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at" / 1000000.0)) = 2020
  GROUP BY 1
)
SELECT 
  m."sale_month",
  pr."name"                           AS "product_name_lowest_profit",
  m."lowest_profit"
FROM month_min                 m
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
  ON DATE_TRUNC('month', TO_TIMESTAMP_NTZ(oi."created_at" / 1000000.0)) = m."sale_month"
JOIN "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"     pr
  ON pr."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE (pr."retail_price" - pr."cost") = m."lowest_profit"
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
ORDER BY m."sale_month" ASC
LIMIT 20;
```

The ten queries above move from basic data inspection (#1–#3) to date exploration (#4–#5), then to profit calculation and month‑level aggregation (#6–#8), and finally to identifying the exact low‑profit product names for every month of the year 2020 (#9–#10).
